    "durationMs": 130936,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified against every requirement.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/` — FastAPI 0.115 app with SQLAlchemy 2.0 (`psycopg` v3 driver, URL read from `DATABASE_URL`, never hard-coded) and pydantic-settings\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — migration creating the `links` table (unique indexed `code`, `url` TEXT, `clicks` counter, `created_at` for ordering)\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head`, then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section; `requirements.txt` pins the installed versions\n\n**Key behaviors, all confirmed by 29 passing tests plus a live end-to-end check:**\n- POST/GET `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` with exact status codes: 201, 200, 302 (Location = stored URL), 404, 409 (duplicate custom code), 422 (malformed JSON, invalid/missing url, invalid code) — every error is JSON with an `error` field via custom exception handlers\n- URLs stored and returned byte-for-byte unchanged; codes validated as 4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores; generated codes are random 7-char, collision-retried\n- Clicks increment atomically (`UPDATE ... clicks + 1`), exactly once per redirect\n- Persistence proven: created a link, redirected, killed the server, restarted via `sh start.sh` — the link and its click count of 1 survived\n\nI truncated my test data afterward, so the database has the schema applied and zero rows, and port 8000 is free for the automated suite."
